      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FISHY BUSINESS (6) was strongly supported last start when a short priced favourite and duly saluted winning by 2.5 lengths at Bendigo in a handy 24.41. Awkwardly drawn but has the ability and in winning form. Has a very good strike-rate from this draw, with two wins from four starts. Shapes as a top winning chance on latest effort. NIKITA BALE (1) has shown good improvement at her last two starts, most recently finishing 3rd at Traralgon over 425m. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings six times from 12 attempts. Expected to feature again. WARRIOR TOMMY (5) has shown good improvement at his last two starts, rewarded with a win last time at Sale over 435m. Can make it two on the bounce. TSU'TEY (3) gets a chance to improve on an unplaced run at his latest outing at this circuit.",
